Cell["\<\
The above graph indicates that the density distribution moves forward in \
space as time progresses.  Specifically, the upstream density is higher (i.e. \
lower velocity) and the downstream density is lower (i.e. higher velocity).  
It is expected that the low density (i.e. high velocity) cars which are out \
front will continue to pull ahead of the high density (i.e. low velocity) \
cars that are following behind.  The above graph illustrates that the region \
of density transition between high density and low density will continue to \
grow over time.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"372aa6ed-b9d1-4787-ae25-ff14f1955026"],

