Cell["\<\
The above graph indicates that the density distribution moves forward in \
space as time progresses.  Specifically, the downstream density is higher \
(i.e. lower velocity) and the upstream density is lower (i.e. higher \
velocity).  Observe that the high speed (i.e. low density) cars catch up with \
the low speed (i.e. high density) cars.  Therefore, the interval between high \
and low density decreases with time.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"37d0f4e7-a8d0-4040-a066-9cda712753df"],

Cell["Examine the velocity at each location and time:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"59ac224f-3eea-411a-94fe-9b04a3de80a3"],

