Cell["\<\
The above graph illustrates that the high density region migrates backwards \
in time.  The reason for this is that at higher densities (i.e. very low \
velocities) the highway begins to fill with cars.  This is a classic example \
of bumper to bumper traffic.  Because the high density (i.e. low speed) cars \
are upstream from the low density (i.e. high speed) cars, then the transition \
interval between high and low density will widen with time.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"081adbab-0641-4742-8203-f9b290248186"],

Cell["Examine the velocity at each location and time:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b4f1164-8ed7-4aeb-9b2f-7fbeff6ce147"],

